{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\xi/R$", "MATH_0003": "$U = \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\underline{\\xi} : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\underline{\\xi}$", "MATH_0007": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0008": "$[U/R] \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0010": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\to [U/R] = \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\xi$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-RS-implies-S1-S2}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-versal-object-existence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-minimal-versal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-construction}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-groupoid-in-functors-construction}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-prorepresentable-groupoid-in-functors-construction}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e8377f2efa44452384e8c5a24770d7b8f389b8bee3b7f15c7c9f4c5fa9dfa5cf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c7aa0693ff59342f0180402167788f2dd1e73455f1d66e602dfcd416c67eaf22", "source_text": "As <MATH_0001> is a deformation category it satisfies (S1) and (S2), see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthere exists a versal formal object. By\nLemma <REF_0003>\nthere exists a minimal versal formal object <MATH_0002> as in the statement\nof the lemma. Setting\n<MATH_0003> the\nassociated map <MATH_0004> is smooth (this is\nthe definition of a versal formal object).\nLet <MATH_0005> be the groupoid in functors constructed in\nLemma <REF_0004>\nfrom the map <MATH_0006>. By\nLemma <REF_0005>\nwe see that <MATH_0007> is a smooth groupoid in functors and that\n<MATH_0008> is an equivalence. By\nLemma <REF_0006>\nwe see that <MATH_0009> is prorepresentable.\nFinally, <MATH_0010> is minimal because <MATH_0011>\ncorresponds to the minimal versal formal object <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:31840f89b7f80106108f937b5ebe203ba08241f11ab50bb52df0687711cfdd92", "unit_id": "tag:06L2:proof"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cc951c79e6def3f4c5c58e646d5a652f0a454afdc34d024203c64514fa7f4fa3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nPresentations by minimal prorepresentable groupoids in functors satisfy the\nfollowing uniqueness property.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4750845706204cec58f0cb1dc4c09375ef148a97b45bbf81eaa59f50a44694ce", "unit_id": "tag:06TD:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$(U', R', s', t', c')$", "MATH_0006": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0007": "$(U', R', s', t', c')$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-minimal-presentations-equivalent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:174d4089c4b0240166527cd9433601e6569df14fd2f48b7e234911d3f4cca293", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5bc0c84c25a40d8a8b577fb36b0bdacb6a42b78a6f85b2148ad298db62bdff8e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be category cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0002>. Assume there exist presentations of\n<MATH_0003> by minimal smooth prorepresentable groupoids\nin functors <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>.\nThen <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> are isomorphic.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:45ceec7e76d45dbfc00b7a4dd9cccad768f2082fdc579d0d8efaffeb52aeabf9", "unit_id": "tag:06L3:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06TD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$[U/R] \\to [U'/R']$", "MATH_0002": "$[U/R]$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-minimal-prorepresentable-groupoid-equivalence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-quotient}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3fc0812561585f52811ff55a16ba4eb7e5d0557a27fdca3483d7d6b717e6a815", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e1ab0a6d5e1a15f2acf1dc403f09098abd6a9af1f889c942b043d8678aa34305", "source_text": "Follows from\nLemma <REF_0001>\nand the observation that a morphism\n<MATH_0001> is the same thing as a morphism\nof groupoids in functors (by our explicit construction of <MATH_0002> in\nDefinition <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5d02241cf1a0e5944bd7442bdd99721bd4d4930c06b70d4a51e6959832083d3c", "unit_id": "tag:06L3:proof"}
